# Tick commands: the watch, run-all and bell buttons on the debug toolbar
# (also "IC10 Bench: ..." in the command palette) while stopped.
# Set a breakpoint on "move Phase 1" (it runs once, at the start), then:
# - Step Tick: on to this chip's next turn. The first one waits out the sleep
#   (4 ticks). After that, one tick each.
# - Run N Ticks: try 10. World in Variables shows the tick count.
# - Run Until Event: pick "dusk" (tick 20; the light comes on in that tick),
#   "drain" (every 15 ticks), or "generator" (when the charge drops below 2500).
alias Phase r15
alias Sensor d0
alias Light d1
alias Battery d2
define Freezing 273
define Spare 2000
move Phase 1
sleep 2 # 4 ticks of 0.5 s
move Phase 2
loop:
l r0 Sensor Temperature
slt r1 r0 Freezing # night
l r2 Battery Charge
sgt r3 r2 Spare # and charge to spare
and r1 r1 r3
s Light On r1
yield
j loop
